(** What Soma takes add.wasm, next to this file, to be: built from
    rust/add (rust/build.sh), it exports add and fib, of i64s, and hypot
    and half, of an f64 and an f32. Here add and fib are of whole numbers,
    N: each call checks it, and a number the module gives that an N
    cannot hold, a negative one, is a run-time error that says so; hypot
    and half are of floats, which an f32 rounds. *)

add : N -> N -> N.
fib : N -> N.
hypot : float -> float -> float.
half : float -> float.
